# scripts/scraper-wake.crontab — item 7 part B.
#
# The wake schedule for the IPODhan scraper, in IST (the VPS crontab runs in
# IST; the scraper process itself is started TZ=UTC by the deploy script and
# does its own IST arithmetic in scraper/src/scheduler/due-step-cycle.ts).
#
# This file is the SSOT for the cron lines. It is NOT installed automatically —
# a crontab is a production mutation. Install it by hand with the recipe in
# docs/ops/prod-ops-recipes.md ("Item 7: installing the scraper wake crontab").
# scraper/tests/unit/scheduler/job-membership.test.ts reads this file and holds
# it in agreement with JOB_STEPS, so the schedule and the code cannot drift.
#
# Nothing here kills anything. scraper-wake.sh starts a cycle only when one is
# not already running; the authoritative skip is the Redis cycle lock inside
# the scraper.
#
# Replace /root/ipodhan/current-prod with the release path for the slot.

# data — discovery, aggregators, GMP. 00:00 / 08:00 / 14:00 IST.
0 0,8,14 * * *   /bin/bash /root/ipodhan/current-prod/scripts/scraper-wake.sh data
# documents — the document pass. Its OWN job on its OWN Redis lock (owner,
# 2026-09-11: "its own lock and never delays the live-figure job"), and
# deliberately outside market hours. 01:00 and 19:00 IST are the implementer's
# choice of two such slots: clear of 10:00-18:30, of the 20:00 GMP pull and of
# the 22:00 closed-IPO job.
0 1,19 * * *     /bin/bash /root/ipodhan/current-prod/scripts/scraper-wake.sh documents
# live figures — subscription + demand graph, gated on market hours and on a
# non-zero OPEN count. Every 30 min 10:00-18:00, plus the 18:30 half of
# OD-19's "10:00-18:30".
*/30 10-18 * * * /bin/bash /root/ipodhan/current-prod/scripts/scraper-wake.sh live
30 18 * * *      /bin/bash /root/ipodhan/current-prod/scripts/scraper-wake.sh live
# closed-IPO backlog (item 17) — 22:00 IST. Carries GMP's late-evening pull.
0 22 * * *       /bin/bash /root/ipodhan/current-prod/scripts/scraper-wake.sh closed
# GMP weekend evening pull — Saturday and Sunday 20:00 IST. The owner asked for
# "one evening pull on Saturday and Sunday" and did not name an hour; 20:00 is
# the implementer's choice, after the grey market's active evening window and
# clear of the 22:00 closed-IPO job so two wakes do not land in one minute.
0 20 * * 6,0     /bin/bash /root/ipodhan/current-prod/scripts/scraper-wake.sh gmp
